{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Types of Server"}, {"type": "position", "content": 1}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 2}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when talking about the different types of servers."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Build the application installation program, using IT development tools available in the market, based on solution architecture features.  Understands the concepts of server, its characteristics and its relation with operating systems."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.  Exchanges simple information on the operating systems, server operating systems and relevant information related with the user manual."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n6le02ob01re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Questions Within Sentences  How to / Where to / What to + Verb"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You can use question words followed by the infinitive of a verb to ask for information. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "This pattern is sometimes followed by certain verbs or phrases. Some of them are as follows:<br/> <ul> <li>Learn</li> <li>Discuss</li> <li>Have information on</li> <li>Know</li> <li>Think about</li> <li>Give an idea of</li> </ul> Always use the base form of the verb in this pattern.<br/><br/>  For example:<br/><br/>  <ul> <li>Learn how <span class=\"strong\">to code</span></li> <li>Discuss what <span class=\"strong\">to install first</span></li> <li>Have information on where <span class=\"strong\">to go</span></li> <li>Know how <span class=\"strong\">to reply</span></li> <li>Think about what <span class=\"strong\">to choose</span></li> <li>Give an idea of what <span class=\"strong\">to connect</span></li> </ul>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "This is not an easy task, you need to be prepared to know how to do it."}, {"type": "example", "content": " Who can tell me how to differentiate them?"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Types of Servers"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "A server is an important component of a computer; it allows it to connect to a network and makes interaction possible."}, {"type": "text", "content": "There are different types of servers, each of them is designed with a specific purpose and works on a different way.<br/> There are five main types of servers: Database, application, print, Internet, and transaction servers.<br/> Take a look at the table below to understand the main concepts about it."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Server Type</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Description</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Database Server</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"As its name suggests, this type of server is in charge of storing and handling data. It also requests data and controls database management. <br /><br />\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Application Server</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"This is a server program that defines the business logic or the domain. Thanks to this type of server, the software installation in each workstation is not necessary. Moreover, this server is generally divided into three parts: the Tier (web browser to user), the Tier (business logic app to local network), and the Tier (back-end to large server). <br /> <br />\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Print Server</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It provides shared access to printers, managing all printers connected to a network. <br /> <br />\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Internet Server</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It is a computer connected to the internet. It exchanges data by loading information from a disk to a browser. There are different types of internet servers, such as file, DNS, mail, gopher, and news servers. <br /> <br />\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Transaction Server</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"This type of sever handles the operations of software on a network or the internet. Most of the time, transaction servers are composed by particular hardware, software, and networks, which make possible the effective completion of transactions. <br /> <br />\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "There are five main types: database, application, print, the Internet, and transaction servers. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "The database server, which is a computer program, provides services to other computers."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "business logic "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a code that makes it possible for a database to work "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Then, we have application servers, which provide the business logic or domain."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le02ob01aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "client "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a workstation on a network "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The database server, which is a computer program, provides services to other computers (or clients)."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le02ob01aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "ensure "}, {"type": "definition", "content": " to make sure "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Finally, there are transaction servers, which ensure users will get the data requested."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le02ob01aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "network "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a system or group of elements connected"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: A server is a component of a network, which provides computers access to the internet or to a network."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le02ob01aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "provide "}, {"type": "definition", "content": " to give or supply  "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  A server is a component of a network, which provides computers access to the internet or to a network.  "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le02ob01aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "serve"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to work for someone else  "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: This means, that a server is a special-purpose computer which serves other computers which are also called clients."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le02ob01aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Look for more information about the different types of servers. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Identify the most important characteristics of the types of servers.  "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write a dialogue talking about the types of servers."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Use the grammar and the vocabulary related to this lesson."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share your dialogue with your class."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I look for more information about the different types of servers. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I identify the most important characteristics of the types of servers. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write a dialogue talking about the types of servers. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I use the grammar and the vocabulary related to this lesson and share my dialogue with my class."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I share my findings with the class."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "welcome", "id": 0, "contents": [{}]}, {"template_override": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"time": "100", "image": "enpe8n6le02ob01re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<span class=\"strong\"> Teacher:</span> Today, we'll talk about the types of servers. Let's start by giving a general definition and describing the types of servers. <br />\n<span class=\"strong\"> Sam:</span> In general terms, a server is a component of a network, which provides computers access to the internet or to a network. This means, that a server is a special-purpose computer which serves other computers which are also called clients. <br />\n<span class=\"strong\"> Teacher:</span> And, who can tell me how to identify a server? <br />\n<span class=\"strong\"> Lea:</span> Actually, a traditional computer can be programmed to be a server. It's not crucial to have specific hardware, but it is necessary to have the correct software installed. This is not a simple task, but you need to know how to do it correctly."}, {"time": "46500", "image": "enpe8n6le02ob01re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<span class=\"strong\"> Teacher:</span> That's correct. Now, let's move to the types of servers. Who can tell me how to differentiate them? <br />\n<span class=\"strong\"> Sam:</span> There are many types of servers implemented on a network. However, there are five main types: database, application, print, the Internet, and transaction servers. <br />\n<span class=\"strong\"> Lea:</span> The database server, which is a computer program, provides services to other computers (or clients) based on a client-server model. It's considered as the most popular type. This one is regularly used by companies to store their database catalogs. Then, we have application servers, which provide the business logic or domain."}, {"time": "91000", "image": "enpe8n6le02ob01re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<span class=\"strong\"> Sam:</span> Print servers are in charge of controlling all printers in a network. Internet servers are specialized computers, which allow other computers to connect to the Internet. Finally, there are transaction servers, which ensure users will get the data requested; it basically operates only when users request specific data. <br />\n<span class=\"strong\"> Teacher:</span> To conclude, remember all servers are designed to accomplish a specific function, and the software or hardware may change from server to server."}], "coverimg": "enpe8n6le02ob01re2img01.jpg", "audiosrc": "enpe8n6le02ob01re2aud01"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "type": "audio", "_data": [], "id": 1, "title": ""}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about the server.   "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "  I can describe the different types of server."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "  I can tell differences among the different types of server."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "How can computers connect to the internet? "}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "Why is it important to have a safe connection?"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}], "allowed_attempts": 2}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "content": "Ask your partner:"}, {"type": "free_type_text_area", "content": "Getting Familiarized with Servers"}], "img_path": "", "id": 0}, {"stimuli_ids": [1], "template_override": 1, "questions": [{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "type": "question"}], "responses": [{"correct": 0, "selected": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "id": 0}, {"correct": 1, "selected": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "id": 1}], "id": 0}], "type": "STI", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " Listen to a class about Information Systems."}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Content"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}, {"type": "text", "content": ""}], "correct_feedback": "", "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}, {"type": "text", "content": ""}], "allowed_attempts": 2}}, {"contents": [{"type": "skill", "content": "Listening"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Reading"}], "type": "learning_skills"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Instructions: Click on the play button to listen to the audio."}], "type": "post_instructions"}], "id": 1}, {"stimuli_ids": [], "template_override": 1, "questions": [{"